# Justified exceptions to the boundary guard (.githooks/boundary-guard).
#
# Format - the reason is part of the syntax, not decoration:
#
#     path/or/glob        # why this file passes the clone test
#
# An entry WITHOUT a '#' reason is ignored by the guard, so it grants nothing.
# That is deliberate: this file is the known weak point of the construction, and
# a bare list of paths would turn it into the dumping ground ADR-025 warns about.
#
# The reason should answer the clone test, not restate the file's purpose:
#   good  # container-internal paths only; the host side is always under /opt/mora02
#   bad   # needed for the build
#
# Shell globs are allowed (config/foo/*). Paths are relative to the repo root.
#
# Empty on purpose. Entries are added when a real false positive shows up, never
# in advance - an exception for a case that never occurred hides the next one.

.githooks/boundary-guard	# the guard's own marker documentation; it names host paths in comments in order to recognise them, and configures nothing
config/dify-ssrf-proxy/*	# container-internal squid config: /var/log and /etc paths live inside the container, and the RFC 1918 entries are ACL ranges describing the docker network, not addresses of this machine
scripts/system/mora02-scheduled-publish.service	# clone test passed (ADR-025): paths under /opt/mora02 only, values from docker/.env, names neither a user nor an address
scripts/system/mora02-scheduled-publish.timer	# clone test passed, see the matching .service
scripts/install-llm-switch.sh	# clone test passed: the units it writes reference only /opt/mora02 paths and name no user, host or address - same construction as mora02-scheduled-publish.service. It installs an application feature, it does not operate this machine
scripts/system/nvidia-persistence.service	# clone test passed: no user, no host path, no address - just 'nvidia-smi -pm 1'. The GPU is part of the system definition (ADR-025), so it stays in the public repository
scripts/llm-bench-tools.py	# clone test passed: the one host marker is a hint in an error message naming llm-switch.path - a unit this repo installs itself via scripts/install-llm-switch.sh, which is listed above for the same reason. Every other path is container-internal or a service named in docker-compose.yml; the results directory was moved out to MORA02_BENCH_OUT
